
-- hvac-nouns.l4 -- the nouns shared by every other module.
--
-- Subject: the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning
-- Systems Law 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3349, p. 182) and its Fees Regulations, in
-- their three vintages.  DECLARE and nothing else: no rules, no directives.
--
-- The membership test (encoding-a-subject, step 4): could a witness of ordinary
-- competence testify to this fact, or does answering it require reading the Act?
-- Only the first kind is a field here.  Where a field is a legal conclusion that
-- somebody else must reach (the Registrar's opinion, the Registrar's recognition),
-- it is a recorded determination, named for who decided it.

-- ============================================================================
-- Part 1.  Nouns for the Fees Regulations and the SimpLEX test table
-- ============================================================================

-- The three vintages of the Fees Regulations are three answers, never merged.
-- A fee lookup takes the vintage as an input.
DECLARE Vintage IS ONE OF
    Draft          -- the SimpLEX screenshot (Figure 4, Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov & Gelbard 2025); never in force
    `As made`      -- Kovetz HaTakanot 11951, 9 July 2025
    `As amended`   -- the 5786 amendment, Kovetz HaTakanot 12383, 4 May 2026

DECLARE `Exam kind` IS ONE OF
    `Theory exam`      -- בחינה עיונית
    `Practical exam`   -- בחינה מעשית

-- What a fee is paid FOR, as the regulations word it.  The draft charges for an
-- APPLICATION for a licence (reg 2(ד), "בעד בקשה לקבלת רישיון"); the regulations as
-- made charge for RECEIVING it (reg 2(ג), "בעד קבלת רישיון"): two rows, because the
-- two wordings name different moments (fork F-F2 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Fee service` IS ONE OF
    `a theory exam`
    `a practical exam`
    `an objection to a theory exam score`      -- fork F-F1: the draft's "ערעור" (appeal) and the enacted "השגה" (objection)
    `an objection to a practical exam score`   --   are one service, an objection to an exam score
    `an application for a licence or its renewal`
    `receiving a licence or its renewal`
    `a request for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or its renewal`
    `a refresher training under section 17`

-- The outcome words printed by the SimpLEX test panel, copied from the screenshot.
DECLARE `SimpLEX outcome` IS ONE OF
    `registration approved`                               -- הרשמה מאושרת
    `the appeal is examined`                              -- הערעור נבדק
    `service suspension`                                  -- השעיית שירות
    `registration rejected, payment must be completed`    -- הרשמה נדחית – חובה להשלים תשלום

DECLARE `SimpLEX request` IS ONE OF
    `registration for an exam`
    `an appeal against an exam score`

-- One SimpLEX scenario: the table's rows do not say which exam an appeal is about
-- or whether a registration is for the theory or the practical exam, so the exam is a
-- field and each row is run against both (fork F-T1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `SimpLEX scenario` HAS
    `the request`              IS A `SimpLEX request`
    `the exam`                 IS AN `Exam kind`
    `the fee was paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The consumer price index values regulation 3 reads, supplied by the caller.
-- The sources contain no index values; none is invented anywhere in this encoding.
DECLARE `Index reading` HAS
    `the year of the November`  IS A NUMBER
    `the index published then`  IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Index series` HAS
    `published in the month before the regulations commenced` IS A NUMBER
    `published in the Novembers`                              IS A LIST OF `Index reading`

-- ============================================================================
-- Part 2.  Nouns for the Law
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Licence grade` IS ONE OF
    `Grade 1`    -- רישיון דרגה 1
    `Grade 2`    -- רישיון דרגה 2
    `Grade 3`    -- רישיון דרגה 3

-- s 63(a)(1) turns on the Fourth Schedule, which is NOT encoded (outside the pinned
-- scope): whether the refrigerant is on its list is a fact supplied by the caller.
DECLARE Refrigerant HAS
    `listed as a flammable refrigerant in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `its use is permitted by law`                              IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2, "מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר" : a system, device or product whose purpose is the
-- removal of heat to the outside of a given substance or space, by means of a refrigerant.
DECLARE `Refrigeration or air-conditioning system` HAS
    `its purpose is the removal of heat to the outside of a given substance or space` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it removes heat by means of a refrigerant`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooling output in kilowatts`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `refrigerant`                                                                     IS A Refrigerant

-- One act of work on a system.  The First Schedule is NOT encoded, so what it says about
-- the act arrives as two facts.
DECLARE `Piece of work` HAS
    `the system worked on`                                                        IS A `Refrigeration or air-conditioning system`
    `the act is of a type fixed in the First Schedule`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is reserved to Grade 3 by Part B item 3(2) or (3) of the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Minister's order under section 3(b) exempts this type of system`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the work`                                                        IS A DATE

DECLARE Licence HAS
    `grade`                                           IS A `Licence grade`
    `the day the validity period began`               IS A DATE
    `a temporary licence for a foreign expert`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of a temporary licence`             IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the current validity period is a renewal`        IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Person doing work` HAS
    `the licence held`                                                             IS A MAYBE Licence
    `acting in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the Law`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2, "תעודת גמר": a document, and what it attests.
DECLARE Certificate HAS
    `issued by the Division`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it attests completion of refrigeration and air-conditioning studies`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it attests successful passing of an exam held by the Division`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the exam held by the Division included a theory exam`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the exam held by the Division included a practical exam`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `issued by the Ministry of Education`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `it attests successful completion of studies in the climate-control track`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---- s 6 and the Second Schedule ------------------------------------------

-- The Second Schedule words two kinds of Division certificate: graded ones ("דרגה 1",
-- "דרגה 2") and one with no grade stated ("תעודת גמר בלימודי קירור ומיזוג אוויר מהאגף").
-- They are kept apart, as the Schedule keeps them apart (fork F-S3).
DECLARE `Division certificate` IS ONE OF
    `a Grade 1 certificate`
    `a Grade 2 certificate`
    `a Grade 3 certificate`
    `a certificate with no grade stated`
    `a certificate from a vocational youth school of the Division`

-- Column A of the Schedule: what the applicant had BEFORE the column B training or studies.
-- (A certificate obtained BY the column B training is recorded under `Training completed`.)
DECLARE `Prior training and experience` HAS
    `holds a Grade 1 licence`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a Grade 2 licence`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the final certificate held from the Division`                                 IS A MAYBE `Division certificate`
    `the climate-control certificate held from the Ministry of Education, in study units` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `registered as a certified air-conditioning technician`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as a certified air-conditioning practical engineer`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed a study programme that includes the supplementary course`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `years of cumulative experience within the three years before the application` IS A NUMBER
    `years of cumulative experience within the seven years before the application` IS A NUMBER

-- What the applicant has completed by way of column B training.  "Up to N hours" in
-- column B is a ceiling on the training the Division may require, not an amount the
-- applicant must reach, so hours are not recorded (fork F-S2).
DECLARE `Training completed` HAS
    `a Division training conferring the final certificate of Grade 1`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Division training conferring the final certificate of Grade 2`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Division training conferring the final certificate of Grade 3`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Division training conferring a final certificate in refrigeration and air-conditioning studies with no grade stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the climate-control certificate obtained from the Ministry of Education, in study units` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `an adult`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- fork F-L1: "בגיר" is not defined in the sources, so a recorded fact, not an age
    `an Israeli citizen or a resident of Israel`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted, or the subject of a pending indictment, for a criminal offence`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence sought`                                                                 IS A `Licence grade`
    `the date of the application`                                                        IS A DATE
    `prior`                                                                              IS A `Prior training and experience`
    `completed`                                                                          IS A `Training completed`

-- ---- s 7 --------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Exemption candidate` HAS
    `holds a valid electricity licence of a kind listed in paragraphs (1) to (7) of regulation 7 of the Electricity Regulations (Licences)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid working-at-heights approval under regulations 5 and 6 of the Work at Heights Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---- s 9 --------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Foreign expert` HAS
    `applying from a foreign state`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooling output in kilowatts of the system he was invited to work on`            IS A NUMBER
    `authorised to perform such work in a foreign state`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the application for the temporary licence`                          IS A DATE
    `the latest date on which he installed or maintained similar systems`            IS A MAYBE DATE
    `recognised by the Registrar as a reputed and renowned expert`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---- s 16 and s 17 ---------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Change of details` HAS
    `the date of the change`                               IS A DATE
    `the date the Registrar was told`                      IS A MAYBE DATE
    `told in the manner the Registrar directed`            IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Refresher training attended` HAS
    `the date`                                                               IS A DATE
    `the hours`                                                              IS A NUMBER
    `under the supervision of the Ministry`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the licensee's field of practice under the licence`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a date the Registrar directed`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licensee met its requirements`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 17(b): the Registrar's additional, specific requirement.
DECLARE `Additional training requirement` HAS
    `the Registrar consulted the Council`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar found circumstances that justify the requirement`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar found participation necessary to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice was given a reasonable time before the training`                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 17(f): publication of trainings.
DECLARE `Publication of a training` HAS
    `published on the Ministry's website`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `published a reasonable time before`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- ============================================================================
-- Part 3.  Parties and acts, for the regulative rules
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Party under the Law` IS ONE OF
    `the Registrar`
    `the licensee`
    `the Director of the Vocational Training Division`
    `the person doing the work`

DECLARE `Act under the Law` IS ONE OF
    `perform work on the system`
    `give the licence to the applicant`
    `give a temporary Grade 3 licence to the foreign expert`
    `renew the temporary licence`
    `give an exemption from the electrical chapter of the training`
    `give an exemption from the working-at-heights chapter of the training`
    `publish the instructions for applying for an exemption`
    `tell the Registrar of the change in details`
    `take part in refresher training in the last year of the licence`
    `require participation in a specific training`
    `extend the validity of the licence`
    `ensure that refresher trainings exist and are available`
    `publish the refresher trainings on the Ministry's website`

-- The Fees Regulations have one duty on an official: regulation 3(b).
DECLARE `Party under the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour`

DECLARE `Act under the Fees Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update`
